{"archetypes":[{"name":"stall-layer-clearing","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Item 4 hinges on extending clear-stall across ship-pr, finalize, and session layers plus Step 18a/18a.5 prompt-side continuation with --in-memory-stall-tracking false without broad write-final-report clearing.","prompt_body":"Trace every STALL_TRACKING read and write path the plan touches: current clear-stall only rewrites ship-pr-state.sh, normalize-outcome still consults four layers, and SKILL.md Step 18a.5 currently passes ambient in-memory stall. Verify the plan specifies all-or-nothing CLEARED semantics, symlink and syntax preflight for each durable layer, and that recovery-success clearing is wired only in Step 18a while write-final-report.sh stays read-only. Flag any missing helper reuse, partial-clear success paths, or prompt-side gaps that would leave stale durable stall blocking escalation-success reporting. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bail-token-surface-audit","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Items 2 and 5 require identical normalized tokens across ci-wait.sh, ci_monitor.py, ci.py, config.py, and stall-recovery-report runtime_bail_token_lines with ci-decide pass-through unchanged but no longer scraped for the Tier B union.","prompt_body":"Enumerate every machine BAIL_REASON emission and pass-through in the in-scope CI wait stack and stall-recovery bail union, comparing repo evidence to the five new CI wait tokens and config-backed decide tokens. Check that ci_monitor poll_ci still has prose strings today, that ci-wait trap defaults and ci-decide forwarded reasons are covered, and that moving the union to config.STALL_RECOVERY_BAIL_REASON_TOKENS plus safe_bail_reason_value lint cannot drop tokens presently sourced only from ci-decide.sh awk scraping. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"launcher-sidecar-failclosed","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Item 1 centralizes resolve_launcher_exit with .done-first precedence and max(process_rc,1) when metadata is missing on non-zero wrapper exit, but multiple callers today parse stdout only or default missing LAUNCHER_EXIT to 0.","prompt_body":"Audit each in-scope launcher-exit consumer against the proposed resolve_launcher_exit contract: plain-integer .done sidecars, valid LAUNCHER_EXIT in captured text, process_rc fail-closed when metadata is absent or invalid, and rc=0 plus missing metadata still meaning success. Confirm make_conflict_launch_fn, ci_monitor _make_default_launch_fn, and read_launcher_exit callers pass wrapper returncode and stderr-inclusive capture where needed, and that no plan step leaves a stdout-only parser on the hot path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
